    RESULT dismiss_resolve_recreate      FAIL {"postDismissBannerAbsent":false,"postDismissStored":false,...}
    RESULT dismiss_then_reload_unchanged FAIL {"dismissedTookEffect":false,"bannerAbsent":false,"regionEmpty":false,...}
    RESULT guard_directions              FAIL {"unrelatedWrites":0,"changedWrites":0,"clearingEmpty":false}
    SUMMARY SOME_FAILED                                  NOOP2_EXIT=1
  All three checks red, as claimed. Worth naming the mechanism: the harness
  carries its own anti-vacuity sentinels (postDismissBannerAbsent,
  postDismissStored, dismissedTookEffect at warnings_dom_harness.js:210-211
  and :258-259) which assert the dismissal ACTUALLY took effect before the
  rest of the sequence is allowed to mean anything. Without them a
  do-nothing script would coast through dismiss_resolve_recreate, because a
  fresh server render is already internally consistent. Those sentinels are
  exactly what turned C2's first two checks red.

